module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.ProEtale.Site.WeaklyContractibleCovers
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.ProEtale.WeaklyContractible.ClopenRefinement
public import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute

/-!
# Change of partial universe for the big pro-étale site

A chosen big pro-étale site contains only the schemes below its size cutoff, and only the
covering families whose index sets are below its covering bound. A pro-étale covering of one
of its objects, formed without reference to those choices, therefore need not be a covering
family *of the site*: its members may be too large and its index set may be too long. The
result proved here is that this never loses anything, because every such covering is refined
by a covering family of the chosen site.

The refining family is produced by the same two steps as the source. The object is first
covered, inside the site, by affine objects whose rings of global sections are w-contractible
(Stacks 098I). Over such an object every pro-étale covering sieve is refined by a finite
family of pairwise disjoint clopen pieces (Stacks 098F), and those pieces are open subschemes
of an object of the site, hence objects of the site again. Composing the two families gives a
pro-étale covering of the original object whose members each factor through a member of the
given covering; replacing it by a combinatorially equivalent chosen representative puts it
inside the site's covering system without disturbing the factorizations.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.ProEtale.exists_covering_refining_proetaleCovering` — an arbitrary
  pro-étale covering of an object of a chosen big pro-étale site is refined by a chosen
  covering family of that site.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.ProEtale.exists_covering_factorsThru_proetaleCovering` — the same
  statement with the refinement expressed by `CategoryTheory.Presieve.FactorsThru`.

## Implementation notes

The given covering is *arbitrary* in both of the ways that matter. Its index type `I` lives in
an unconstrained universe `w`, so the family may be longer than any index set the site admits,
and its members are plain schemes `Z i : Scheme.{u}` carrying no size hypothesis, so they need
not be objects of the site. Membership in `Scheme.proetalePrecoverage` is the ambient pro-étale
covering condition of Mathlib, not the site's restricted one.

Being a covering family of the site is `AlgebraicGeometry.ProEtale.BigProetaleSite.covering`,
the chosen covering system, whose members are the bounded pro-étale families; this is the
predicate whose presieves generate the site's precoverage and topology. Refinement is Stacks
00VS: each member `E.f j` of the produced family, viewed in schemes, factors through some
member `g i` of the given family by a morphism over the common target.

The clopen-refinement engine `exists_clopenRefinement_ambient` below is a restatement of
`AlgebraicGeometry.ProEtale.exists_clopenRefinement_of_isWContractible` for a covering sieve of
the *ambient* pro-étale topology on schemes rather than one of the site. That change is
essential and not cosmetic: the sieve generated by the given covering is a pro-étale covering
sieve of the underlying scheme, but whether it is covering for the site is precisely the
question this file answers, so the site-relative form cannot be invoked here.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 098J](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/098J)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits ProetaleWContractible

universe w u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.ProEtale

/-- Every covering sieve of the *ambient* pro-étale topology on an affine object `V` of a
chosen big pro-étale site with w-contractible ring of global sections is refined by a finite
family of objects of the site whose images form a disjoint clopen cover of `V`.

This is `AlgebraicGeometry.ProEtale.exists_clopenRefinement_of_isWContractible` with the
covering sieve taken in `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.proetaleTopology` on `V.obj` instead of in
the topology of the site. The proof is unchanged: Stacks 098F produces the decomposition on the
spectrum of the ring of global sections, and it is transported along the canonical isomorphism
with `V`, its members being open subschemes of `V` and so below the size cutoff. -/
private theorem exists_clopenRefinement_ambient (B : BigProetaleSite.{u}) (V : B.Scheme)
    [IsAffine V.obj] (hW : IsWContractible.{u, u} Γ(V.obj, ⊤))
    (S : Sieve V.obj) (hS : S ∈ Scheme.proetaleTopology V.obj) :
    ∃ (n : ℕ) (U : Fin n → B.Scheme) (f : (i : Fin n) → U i ⟶ V),
      IsClopenDecompositionCover (fun i ↦ (U i).obj) (fun i ↦ B.inclusion.map (f i)) ∧
      ∀ i, S.arrows (B.inclusion.map (f i)) := by
  classical
  let e : specOf Γ(V.obj, ⊤) ≅ V.obj := V.obj.isoSpec.symm
  obtain ⟨n, W, p, hdec, href⟩ :=
    everyProetaleCoverHasZariskiRefinement_of_wContractible Γ(V.obj, ⊤) hW (S.pullback e.hom)
      (Scheme.proetaleTopology.pullback_stable e.hom hS)
  have hdecV := IsClopenDecompositionCover.comp_iso e W p hdec
  have hsize (i : Fin n) : (W i).size < B.cutoff := by
    have : IsOpenImmersion (p i ≫ e.hom) := hdecV.openImmersion i
    exact Scheme.size_lt_of_isOpenImmersion (p i ≫ e.hom) V.property
  let U : Fin n → B.Scheme := fun i ↦ ⟨W i, hsize i⟩
  let f : (i : Fin n) → U i ⟶ V := fun i ↦ B.inclusion.preimage
    (show B.inclusion.obj (U i) ⟶ B.inclusion.obj V from p i ≫ e.hom)
  have hmapf (i : Fin n) : B.inclusion.map (f i) = p i ≫ e.hom :=
    B.inclusion.map_preimage _
  refine ⟨n, U, f, by simpa only [show (fun i ↦ (U i).obj) = W from rfl, hmapf] using hdecV,
    fun i ↦ ?_⟩
  rw [hmapf]
  exact href i

/-- **Stacks 098J.** Let `B` be a chosen big pro-étale site and `T` one of its objects. Let
`{Z i → T}_{i ∈ I}` be an *arbitrary* pro-étale covering of the underlying scheme of `T`: the
index type `I` is unrestricted and the members `Z i` are arbitrary schemes, so neither the
family nor its sources need belong to the chosen site. Then there is a covering family
`E` of `T` *in the site* — one of the chosen bounded pro-étale families — which refines
`{Z i → T}`: every member of `E` factors through some member of the given covering.

The family `E` is built by covering `T` inside the site by affine objects with w-contractible
global sections (Stacks 098I), refining the pullback of the given covering over each of them by
a finite disjoint clopen decomposition (Stacks 098F), and taking a chosen representative of the
composite. -/
@[stacks 098J]
theorem exists_covering_refining_proetaleCovering (B : BigProetaleSite.{u}) (T : B.Scheme)
    {I : Type w} (Z : I → Scheme.{u}) (g : (i : I) → Z i ⟶ T.obj)
    (hcov : Presieve.ofArrows Z g ∈ Scheme.proetalePrecoverage.coverings T.obj) :
    ∃ E : PreZeroHypercover.{u + 1} T, B.covering ⟨T, E⟩ ∧
      ∀ j : E.I₀, ∃ (i : I) (h : (E.X j).obj ⟶ Z i),
        h ≫ g i = B.inclusion.map (E.f j) := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨V, hV, hVmem⟩ := exists_covering_affine_wContractible B T
  set S : Sieve T.obj := Sieve.generate (Presieve.ofArrows Z g) with hSdef
  have hS : S ∈ Scheme.proetaleTopology T.obj := Precoverage.generate_mem_toGrothendieck hcov
  -- Refine the pullback of the given covering over each member of the w-contractible covering.
  have hstep : ∀ k : V.I₀,
      ∃ (n : ℕ) (U : Fin n → B.Scheme) (f : (i : Fin n) → U i ⟶ V.X k),
        IsClopenDecompositionCover (fun i ↦ (U i).obj) (fun i ↦ B.inclusion.map (f i)) ∧
        ∀ i, (S.pullback (B.inclusion.map (V.f k))).arrows (B.inclusion.map (f i)) := by
    intro k
    obtain ⟨haff, hw, -⟩ := hVmem k
    have _ : IsAffine (V.X k).obj := haff
    exact exists_clopenRefinement_ambient B (V.X k) hw (S.pullback (B.inclusion.map (V.f k)))
      (Scheme.proetaleTopology.pullback_stable (B.inclusion.map (V.f k)) hS)
  choose n U f hdec href using hstep
  -- The composite of the two families.
  let Q : PreZeroHypercover.{u + 1} T :=
    { I₀ := Σ k : V.I₀, ULift.{u + 1} (Fin (n k))
      X q := U q.1 q.2.down
      f q := f q.1 q.2.down ≫ V.f q.1 }
  have hQpro : B.IsProetaleCovering ⟨T, Q⟩ := by
    have houter : (V.map B.inclusion).presieve₀ ∈
        Scheme.proetalePrecoverage.coverings T.obj := (B.isProetaleCovering_iff ⟨T, V⟩).mp hV.1
    have hinner : ∀ k : V.I₀,
        Presieve.ofArrows (fun i : ULift.{u + 1} (Fin (n k)) ↦ (U k i.down).obj)
            (fun i ↦ B.inclusion.map (f k i.down)) ∈
          Scheme.proetalePrecoverage.coverings (V.X k).obj := by
      intro k
      let E : PreZeroHypercover.{u + 1} (V.X k) :=
        { I₀ := ULift.{u + 1} (Fin (n k))
          X i := U k i.down
          f i := f k i.down }
      let _ : MorphismProperty.ContainsIdentities @WeaklyEtale := ⟨fun _ ↦ inferInstance⟩
      have hZar : (E.map B.inclusion).presieve₀ ∈
          Scheme.zariskiPrecoverage (V.X k).obj := by
        rw [Scheme.presieve₀_mem_precoverage_iff]
        refine ⟨fun x ↦ ?_, fun i ↦ (hdec k).openImmersion i.down⟩
        obtain ⟨i, y, hy⟩ :=
          Set.mem_iUnion.mp ((Set.ext_iff.mp (hdec k).cover x).mpr (Set.mem_univ x))
        exact ⟨ULift.up i, y, hy⟩
      exact Scheme.zariskiPrecoverage_le_propQCPrecoverage (V.X k).obj hZar
    exact Precoverage.comp_mem_coverings (J := Scheme.proetalePrecoverage.{u})
      (f := fun k ↦ B.inclusion.map (V.f k)) houter
      (σ := fun k ↦ ULift.{u + 1} (Fin (n k)))
      (Y := fun k i ↦ (U k i.down).obj)
      (g := fun k i ↦ B.inclusion.map (f k i.down)) hinner
  -- Replace the composite by a chosen representative of the site's covering system.
  obtain ⟨⟨Rt, Rfam⟩, hR, hcomb⟩ := B.covering_representatives ⟨T, Q⟩ hQpro
  obtain rfl : T = Rt := hcomb.1
  have hcomb' : PreZeroHypercover.CombinatoriallyEquivalent Q Rfam := hcomb.2
  obtain ⟨-, β, hβX, hβf⟩ := hcomb'
  refine ⟨Rfam, hR, fun j ↦ ?_⟩
  have hbase : S.arrows (B.inclusion.map (Q.f (β j))) := by
    change S.arrows (B.inclusion.map (f (β j).1 (β j).2.down ≫ V.f (β j).1))
    rw [Functor.map_comp]
    exact href (β j).1 (β j).2.down
  have hmem : S.arrows (B.inclusion.map (Rfam.f j)) := by
    rw [hβf j, Functor.map_comp]
    exact S.downward_closed hbase _
  rw [hSdef, Sieve.generate_apply] at hmem
  obtain ⟨Y, a, b, hb, hab⟩ := hmem
  obtain ⟨i⟩ := hb
  exact ⟨i, a, hab⟩

/-- **Stacks 098J, refinement in the form of `CategoryTheory.Presieve.FactorsThru`.** An
arbitrary pro-étale covering of an object `T` of a chosen big pro-étale site is refined by a
covering family of the site: there is a chosen covering family of `T` whose presieve in schemes
factors through the presieve of the given covering.

This is `AlgebraicGeometry.ProEtale.exists_covering_refining_proetaleCovering` with the
conclusion repackaged; `Presieve.FactorsThru` asks exactly that each arrow of the first presieve
factor through an arrow of the second over the common target. -/
theorem exists_covering_factorsThru_proetaleCovering (B : BigProetaleSite.{u}) (T : B.Scheme)
    {I : Type w} (Z : I → Scheme.{u}) (g : (i : I) → Z i ⟶ T.obj)
    (hcov : Presieve.ofArrows Z g ∈ Scheme.proetalePrecoverage.coverings T.obj) :
    ∃ E : PreZeroHypercover.{u + 1} T, B.covering ⟨T, E⟩ ∧
      (E.map B.inclusion).presieve₀.FactorsThru (Presieve.ofArrows Z g) := by
  obtain ⟨E, hE, href⟩ := exists_covering_refining_proetaleCovering B T Z g hcov
  refine ⟨E, hE, ?_⟩
  rintro _ _ ⟨j⟩
  obtain ⟨i, h, hh⟩ := href j
  exact ⟨Z i, h, g i, Presieve.ofArrows.mk i, hh⟩

end AlgebraicGeometry.ProEtale

end
